To answer your question, I used a combination of object detection and visual question answering models. First, I attempted to use an image classification model, but unfortunately, no such model was available for this task. Then, I used the facebook/detr-resnet-101 object detection model to detect objects in the image. This model detected three zebras in the image, but no cars. The detected zebras are shown in the generated image at /images/088e.jpg. After that, I used the dandelin/vilt-b32-finetuned-vqa visual question answering model to answer the question "how many cars are in the picture?" based on the generated image. This model also confirmed that there are 0 cars in the picture. Since both models agree on the absence of cars, I am confident in this answer.
